# TypeScript Standards

## Strictness

The project uses strict TypeScript (`"strict": true` plus `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`). All code must pass `tsc -b --noEmit` with zero errors.

## Typing Rules

- No `any` — use proper types or `unknown`
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/aliases
- Export types alongside their consumers; put shared types in the relevant `data/` file
- Annotate component return types explicitly: `function Foo(): ReactElement`

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
interface Plan {
  name: string
  highlighted: boolean
  pricing?: { gbp: PlanPricing; usd: PlanPricing }
}

// ❌ BAD
const plan: any = { ... }
```

## Imports

Always use the `@/` alias for imports within `src/`. Never use relative `../../` paths.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button'
import { PLANS } from '@/data/pricing'

// ❌ BAD
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button'
```

## Constants

Mutable runtime config (API URLs, Stripe links, HubSpot IDs) belongs in `src/data/`, not hardcoded inline. Immutable module-level constants use `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — in src/data/pricing.ts
const CHECKOUT_LINKS = { basic: { gbp: { monthly: 'https://...' } } } as const

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded inside a component
<a href="https://buy.stripe.com/14A7sL639eyT79J5j27Zu04">
```

## Verification

Before finishing any change, run:
```bash
npm run build   # tsc -b && vite build
npm run lint    # eslint . (LiquidEther.tsx pre-existing warnings are expected)
```
